17:["$","main",null,{"id":"top","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"border-b border-ink/10 bg-surface/40","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 py-10 sm:px-8","children":[["$","$Ld",null,{"href":"/operating-system","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-mute transition hover:text-accent","children":"← All chapters"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-5 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-accent","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"rounded-full bg-accent/12 px-2.5 py-0.5","children":"Chapter 28"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-mute","children":["· ",17," min read · illustrated"]}]]}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"mt-3 font-hand text-5xl font-bold leading-tight text-ink sm:text-6xl","children":"Files & Directories"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-lg text-mute","children":"The named, persistent byte-stream you have been reading and writing all along, and the machinery hiding behind the name"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 flex max-w-2xl flex-col gap-3","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-[1.02rem] leading-[1.75] text-ink/85","children":"In the last two chapters we lived down at the level of the disk: platters, sectors, and the numbered blocks an SSD or spinning drive actually understands. That world is unforgiving, a disk has no idea what a \"file\" is, no concept of a name, and no notion of who owns what. It stores block 5,281,904 and will happily hand it back, and nothing more. Yet you have never once written a program that talks in block numbers. You open \"config.json\", you read a few kilobytes, you close it. Between those two worlds sits one of the most successful abstractions in all of computing: the file."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"text-[1.02rem] leading-[1.75] text-ink/85","children":"This chapter is about that abstraction from the outside, the part you, the programmer, actually touch. A file is a named, persistent stream of bytes; a directory is a special file that maps names to files; and permissions decide who may do what. We will walk through opening a file and following the descriptor down through the kernel’s tables to the bytes on disk, take apart the inode that stores everything about a file except its name, see why a directory is \"just a file\" and how a path is resolved one component at a time, and untangle hard links from symbolic links once and for all."}],["$","p","2",{"className":"text-[1.02rem] leading-[1.75] text-ink/85","children":"Everything here is the user-facing contract; the next chapter opens the box and shows how a real file system implements it on top of those raw blocks. Throughout, we keep an engineer’s eye on the parts that bite in production, descriptor leaks, unsafe writes, path traps, and the fact that the database you run every day is, underneath, a small number of very large files with their own private structure."}]]}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto flex max-w-6xl gap-10 px-5 py-12 sm:px-8","children":[["$","nav",null,{"className":"sticky top-8 hidden h-fit w-56 shrink-0 lg:block","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-3 font-hand text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"On this page"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-1.5 text-sm","children":[["$","li","01-the-file-abstraction",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#01-the-file-abstraction","className":"flex gap-2 rounded-md px-2 py-1 text-mute transition hover:bg-accent/10 hover:text-accent","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent/70","children":"01"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"leading-snug","children":"The file: a named, persistent stream of bytes"}]]}]}],"$L21","$L22","$L23","$L24","$L25","$L26","$L27"]}]]}],"$L28"]}],"$L29"]}]
